Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: bind Nova motion vectors to the committed display frame

Base: MiCode/vendor_opensource_display-drivers
      1f1cd9c1b674014ae6ca324ffea12c96e121d6e1
Reference: Athens stock 406 msm_drm.ko
           f852df29151bc376aca0ff9ff6f707d7ba1c3d56

Give each atomic connector state ownership of its one-shot EMV packet.
Send from the existing display worker after the matching encoder has
committed. A subsequent kickoff on the same active connector can
finish its predecessor's fresh packet while the old image is still on
screen. Classify contention, expired data, cancellation and transport
errors. Never build up a frame queue.

Verify against the pinned source using verify-emv-commit.py alongside
this patch. An Athens module additionally requires matching kernel
build inputs and the complete Novatek D2 driver, which the public
display snapshot omits.

